# Patched Ouster ROS 2 driver — fetched at image-build time by docker/Dockerfile.runtime
# (tools/fetch_upstream.py, using vcstool). Nothing upstream is committed to this repo;
# it lives only in the build and in a gitignored src/ for local dev. The SDK override is
# pinned independently in ouster-sdk.repos and applied by the same fetch helper.
#
# `version` MUST be a full commit SHA (never a branch) for reproducible patched builds.
# Keep rigging.yaml `msgs.source.repo` and `msgs.source.ref` matched to url/version here
# (the fleet-ros-msgs overlay for ouster_sensor_msgs), or source provenance drifts.
# Based on upstream 0.15.1 (73cf036); keeps each queued scan's timestamps with its data
# and adds regression coverage for backlog, dropped packets, slot reuse, and
# complete 128-beam scans. Raw packet QoS uses explicit bounded queues, with
# reliable replay and regressions for both maximum-rate legacy lidar modes.
# Live raw publishing uses bounded per-stream workers, isolating UDP reception
# from subscriber backpressure, with loopback and sensor-callback regressions.
# The optional mask image is decoded by a bundled stb_image, and TIFF by libtiff, so the
# driver links no OpenCV.
# Backports upstream f4c83a6 + bbe9a89: normalize destagger shifts per row
# instead of dividing per point, with negative-shift validation and 96 original-cloud
# equivalence cases. Also hoists organized output-row indexing out of the point loop.
# Point fields, layout and sensor settings are unchanged.
# Images process only demanded channels by default, with image_always_process as an override.
# Image scratch/span reuse and direct PointCloud2 writes preserve output fields/layout.
# Optional organized_cloud_crop retains fields/row alignment while reducing cloud width
# to the metadata-derived azimuth interval; default full-frame output is unchanged.
# XYZ is fused into the final cloud write; native image reads and selected-ring
# LaserScan extraction avoid intermediate full-frame copies. Telemetry coalescing
# is reset safely across reconfiguration. The ROS default is per-packet; this service
# supplies a 10 Hz default, with explicit telemetry_max_rate_hz: 0.0 to opt out.
# Retention branch: perf/cpu-loop-telemetry-20261113.
# See README "Updating upstream".
#
# A LAN mirror must cover both manifests and any upstream submodules; retain all pinned refs.
repositories:
  ouster-ros:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/christomaszewski/ouster-ros.git
    version: f80d05c7a1255a365cfa2a36e218dd988a077b59
